  "instance_name": "gluten_allergy",
  "label": "Gluten allergy and celiac disease",
  "description": "A medical condition where the immune system reacts to gluten, a protein found in wheat, barley, and rye. Celiac disease is an autoimmune disorder triggered by gluten ingestion, causing damage to the small intestine. Gluten sensitivity is a non-celiac condition with similar symptoms. These conditions are not new and have been recognized for centuries, though awareness and diagnosis have increased in recent decades due to better medical understanding and testing.",
